Below is a **clean, 2026-ready, production SFTP configuration guide** for **RHEL 9 and Ubuntu 24.04**, from **basic → advanced → enterprise hardening**, with correct modern OpenSSH practices.

---

# 🟢 1. What is modern SFTP (2026)?

SFTP runs inside SSH:

```text
SFTP = SSH subsystem (internal-sftp)
```

So:

* ❌ No FTP server needed (vsftpd/proftpd not used)
* ✅ Uses OpenSSH (`sshd`)
* 🔐 Fully encrypted

---

# 🟢 2. INSTALL OPENSSH (BASIC SETUP)

## RHEL 9

```bash
sudo dnf update -y
sudo dnf install -y openssh-server
sudo systemctl enable --now sshd
```

## Ubuntu 24.04

```bash
sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y openssh-server
sudo systemctl enable --now ssh
```

### Check service

```bash
ss -tulpn | grep ssh
```

---

# 🟢 3. TEST DEFAULT SFTP

```bash
sftp localhost
```

If it connects → SSH/SFTP is working.

---

# 🟡 4. CREATE SFTP USER (BASIC)

```bash
sudo groupadd sftpusers
sudo useradd -m -g sftpusers -s /usr/sbin/nologin sftpuser
sudo passwd sftpuser
```

### Meaning:

* no shell login
* only SFTP allowed

---

# 🟡 5. CREATE DIRECTORY STRUCTURE (CHROOT)

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /sftp/sftpuser/upload
```

### Permissions (VERY IMPORTANT)

```bash
sudo chown root:root /sftp/sftpuser
sudo chmod 755 /sftp/sftpuser

sudo chown sftpuser:sftpusers /sftp/sftpuser/upload
```

### Why?

* chroot folder must be owned by root
* prevents escape from jail

---

# 🟡 6. BASIC SSH CONFIGURATION

Edit config:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

### Add:

```text
Subsystem sftp internal-sftp

PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
```

### Meaning:

* internal-sftp = modern SFTP engine
* disables insecure login methods

---

# 🟠 7. ENABLE CHROOT SFTP (IMPORTANT STEP)

Add at end:

```text
Match Group sftpusers
    ChrootDirectory /sftp/%u
    ForceCommand internal-sftp
    X11Forwarding no
    AllowTcpForwarding no
```

### Effect:

* user is locked inside folder
* cannot access system shell

---

# 🟠 8. VALIDATE CONFIG

```bash
sudo sshd -t
```

(no output = OK)

---

# 🟠 9. RESTART SSH SERVICE

## RHEL 9

```bash
sudo systemctl restart sshd
```

## Ubuntu 24

```bash
sudo systemctl restart ssh
```

---

# 🟠 10. OPEN FIREWALL

## RHEL 9 (firewalld)

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=ssh
sudo firewall-cmd --reload
```

## Ubuntu 24 (ufw)

```bash
sudo ufw allow OpenSSH
sudo ufw enable
```

---

# 🔵 11. CLIENT SETUP (MODERN)

## Install client tools

### RHEL 9

```bash
sudo dnf install -y openssh-clients
```

### Ubuntu 24

```bash
sudo apt install -y openssh-client
```

---

# 🔵 12. GENERATE SSH KEY (MODERN 2026 STANDARD)

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -a 100
```

### Why ed25519?

* faster
* stronger than RSA
* modern standard

---

# 🔵 13. COPY KEY TO SERVER

```bash
ssh-copy-id sftpuser@SERVER_IP
```

---

# 🔵 14. CONNECT USING SFTP

```bash
sftp sftpuser@SERVER_IP
```

---

# 🔵 15. BASIC SFTP COMMANDS

Inside session:

| Command  | Function          |
| -------- | ----------------- |
| ls       | list server files |
| pwd      | server directory  |
| lpwd     | local directory   |
| put file | upload            |
| get file | download          |
| mkdir    | create folder     |
| bye      | exit              |

---

# 🔵 16. NON-INTERACTIVE (AUTOMATION)

```bash
sftp sftpuser@SERVER_IP <<EOF
put file.txt
bye
EOF
```

---

# 🔴 17. ADVANCED SECURITY HARDENING

Edit `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`:

```text
AuthenticationMethods publickey
PermitEmptyPasswords no
MaxAuthTries 3
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2
UseDNS no
```

---

## Strong modern encryption (optional but recommended)

```text
KexAlgorithms curve25519-sha256
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com
```

---

# 🔴 18. SELINUX (RHEL 9 IMPORTANT)

```bash
sudo dnf install -y policycoreutils-python-utils

sudo semanage fcontext -a -t ssh_home_t "/sftp(/.*)?"
sudo restorecon -Rv /sftp
```

Optional fix:

```bash
setsebool -P ssh_chroot_rw_homedirs on
```

---

# 🔴 19. LOGGING & MONITORING

## RHEL 9

```bash
journalctl -u sshd -f
tail -f /var/log/secure
```

## Ubuntu 24

```bash
journalctl -u ssh -f
tail -f /var/log/auth.log
```

---

# 🔴 20. TROUBLESHOOTING

### Permission denied

```bash
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

### Chroot error

* check root ownership of /sftp/user

### SSH config error

```bash
sshd -t
```

